SUMMARY:National Recognition nominations now close on Sunday 11 October
DESCRIPTION:The official page now gives the deadline for submissions as 11:
 59 pm on Sunday 11 October 2026. It was Sunday 4 October.\nThe source says
  nominations received after the deadline cannot be considered.
URL:https://gov.ky/web/mysch/national-recognition-awards
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-7280dcaf5e725506d5bb@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:CSC 2027 registration deadline: 20 November
DESCRIPTION:The Civil Service College registration page lists 20 November 2
 026 for programmes starting in 2027\, including leadership and workplace d
 igital skills.\nConfirmed calendar date only\; closing hour is not stated.
  Confirm admission\, employment eligibility\, course cost and the relevant
  programme before applying.
URL:https://gov.ky/en/web/csc/registration
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-d8edb116518bc7c4664c@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Electricity fuel-charge cap and fuel duty waiver now run to 31 Dece
 mber
DESCRIPTION:Government extended the 2026 Fuel Relief Programme by three mon
 ths. The residential electricity fuel charge stays capped at CI$0.18 per k
 Wh\, and the 100% import-duty waiver on gasoline\, diesel and propane cont
 inues.\nThe waiver removes the Government duty\; it does not set or freeze
  pump prices. The release's example saving is about $70.44 a month on 1\,2
 00 kWh at September's fuel rate.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/government-extends-fuel-relief-prog
 ramme-through-december-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-8bd6288b9b001acfcf1e@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270108
SUMMARY:Duty-free allowance is CI$800 now and CI$1\,000 from 23 November
DESCRIPTION:The standard allowance for returning residents rose from CI$500
  to CI$800 on 1 September. A temporary CI$1\,000 allowance applies for Chr
 istmas travel\, 23 November 2026 to 7 January 2027\, then CI$800 resumes o
 n 8 January.\nFor the summer window the release said the higher allowance 
 applied at the discretion of Customs and Border Control. Check declaration
  rules with CBC before you travel.
URL:https://gov.ky/w/cabinet-approves-increased-duty-allowances-for-returni
 ng-residents
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-e757c8e93cb0e745c3a2@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Free shuttle now links East End and North Side
DESCRIPTION:The Eastern Link is a free four-month public transport pilot th
 at started 1 October. It runs Monday to Saturday\, 7:30 am to 7:30 pm\, no
 t on public holidays. If you transfer to an existing public bus\, the norm
 al bus fare applies.\nThe release names three services and Frank Sound Jun
 ction as the connection to existing buses\; stop lists were attachments no
 t shown on the page. No end date is given beyond four months. The four-mon
 th duration is stated\, but an exact end date is not supplied.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/the-eastern-link-connecting-east-en
 d-and-north-side-to-launch-1-october
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-9688bbb7c79b803ac422@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:Government schools are closed to students from Thursday 15 to Frida
 y 23 October
DESCRIPTION:Two teacher training days on 15 and 16 October run straight int
 o the half-term break of 19 to 23 October. That is seven school days in a 
 row with no classes.\nFrom the approved calendar PDF. The calendar lists n
 o closure on Monday 26 October. Confirm with your child's school.
URL:https://gov.ky/w/cayman-islands-government-schools-2026-2027-school-cal
 endar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-f16a6bcbf5819f88b776@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261229
SUMMARY:Public holidays left this year: 9 November\, 25 December and 28 Dec
 ember
DESCRIPTION:Remembrance Day is Monday 9 November. Christmas Day is Friday 2
 5 December and Boxing Day is observed on Monday 28 December. Government of
 fices close on public holidays.\nThe official 2026 list has no October pub
 lic holiday. Check the Government list before treating another listing as 
 an official holiday.
URL:https://gov.ky/public-holidays
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-816917c94ced5c8ecce3@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
SUMMARY:Cayman Airways' last nonstop New York flight is 19 October
DESCRIPTION:The airline is ending its Grand Cayman to New York JFK nonstop 
 service. The final flight operates on 19 October 2026.\nIf you hold a book
 ing after 19 October\, check it with Cayman Airways. The release does not 
 describe rebooking or refunds.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/cayman-airways-to-conclude-its-new-
 york-service-as-it-prepares-to-blaze-trails-in-new-markets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-947461d7ca255837a1a4@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Police: never share your six-digit WhatsApp code
DESCRIPTION:RCIPS says scammers are taking over local WhatsApp accounts by 
 asking for the six-digit verification code\, then messaging the owner's co
 ntacts for money. Turn on two-step verification\, and call the person befo
 re sending money.\nThe advice to call the person first is ordinary caution
 \, not a quote from the release.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/police-warn-of-ongoing-whatsapp-imp
 ersonation-scams
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-39529a6bfece049587af@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Statistics Office interviewers are visiting about 2\,000 homes: ask
  for the ESO ID card
DESCRIPTION:The Fall Labour Force and Quality of Life surveys began on Sund
 ay 27 September. Trained interviewers carry Economics and Statistics Offic
 e ID cards. To check\, call the ESO on 516-3329 or 949-0940.\nThe notice g
 ives no end date for fieldwork.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/fall-2026-labour-force-survey-and-q
 uality-of-life-survey-starts-sunday
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-dbf669145c1d176037f7@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Driving licence fees changed on 1 September: discounts for longer l
 icences\, reduced fee at 65
DESCRIPTION:Caymanians buying three-\, five- and ten-year licences get 10%\
 , 15% and 20% off. Customers aged 65 or older qualify for the reduced fee\
 , including non-Caymanian seniors. Non-Caymanian full licence fees are abo
 ut three times the Caymanian rate\, down from the eight times first approv
 ed.\nIf you think the wrong fee was applied\, go to a DVDL office with you
 r receipt and ID. The release gives ratios and discounts\, not a full pric
 e list.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/revised-dvdl-fee-structure-effectiv
 e-1-september-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-b7f49efc43dc9b177c82@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Have your say on protecting George Town's Ironwood Forest by 20 Nov
 ember
DESCRIPTION:The National Conservation Council is asking for public comments
  on protecting a 10.3-acre Crown parcel of dry forest in central George To
 wn.\nThe page gives a closing date and no closing hour.
URL:https://publicconsultation.gov.ky/department-of-environment/ironwood-fo
 rest/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-c7e3f1e98b4409728c59@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Cayman Brac: comment on the proposed Bluff Lighthouse National Park
  by 20 November
DESCRIPTION:The National Conservation Council is asking for public comments
  on protecting Crown parcels along the north-eastern Bluff\, including all
  of Long Beach\, while keeping the area open for managed public access.\nT
 he page gives a closing date and no closing hour.
URL:https://publicconsultation.gov.ky/department-of-environment/cayman-brac
 -lighthouse/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-b22165a09218af331ee4@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
SUMMARY:Pirates Week dates: Brac 30 to 31 October\, Grand Cayman 6 to 14 No
 vember\, Little Cayman 20 to 21 November
DESCRIPTION:The Minister reconfirmed the 2026 festival dates for all three 
 islands. Road closures for the Grand Cayman events had not been published 
 when this was checked.\nDates only. Event times\, costs and road closures 
 are not stated in this festival release\; check current official event and
  police notices.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/pirates-week-2026-theme-revealed-sp
 irits-gold-and-glory
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-c564d06b7887c310106a@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:New rules for bringing dogs and cats into Cayman took effect 1 Octo
 ber
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Agriculture revised the conditions for import
 ing dogs and cats. If you travel with a pet or plan to bring one in\, chec
 k the new requirements first. Contact the Department on 947-3090.\nThis en
 try does not summarise the individual requirements. Read the advisory or a
 sk the Department.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/department-of-agriculture-issues-ad
 visory-on-importation-conditions-for-dogs-and-cats-into-the-cayman-islands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-483aac605c5723865954@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Chamber's Mentoring Cayman needs mentors: apply by 30 October
DESCRIPTION:The Chamber of Commerce pairs Year 11 students with professiona
 ls for a six-month programme. It is accepting mentor applications for 2026
 /27 until 30 October.\nA Chamber of Commerce programme\, carried by Radio 
 Cayman. The application form link is in the release.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/mentoring-cayman-seeks-mentors-to-h
 elp-shape-the-future
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-1cf107bbc00312edd654@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:No-cost mammogram in October for CG BritCay Premier and Provident m
 embers
DESCRIPTION:The insurer says members of those two plans can get a mammogram
  at Doctors Hospital with nothing to pay out of pocket during October\, wi
 thout using their annual wellness allowance. Appointments are limited. The
  booking number is in the insurer's notice\; say which plan you are on whe
 n you call.\nA company's offer to its own policyholders\, carried by Radio
  Cayman. Listed because it is a benefit members may not know they have\; i
 t is not an advertisement or an endorsement.
URL:https://www.radiocayman.gov.ky/news/cg-britcay-reintroduces-complimenta
 ry-mammogram-initiative-for-breast-cancer-awareness-month-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-f7522002c7c2393ed95a@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
SUMMARY:Water Authority rates went up 3% from 1 July
DESCRIPTION:The first base-price change in seven years. For Grand Cayman ho
 mes\, the first 12 cubic metres a month (about 3\,200 US gallons) went fro
 m $4.34 to $4.47 per cubic metre.\nThe figure quoted is for the first cons
 umption band in Grand Cayman only. Other bands and the Sister Islands are 
 in the notice.
URL:https://www.waterauthority.ky/water-authority-announces-base-price-adju
 stment
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-c26763f003a02deb168f@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:George Town: water pipe works on Rockshire Drive until about early 
 November
DESCRIPTION:Water Authority works on Rockshire Drive started on 23 Septembe
 r and are expected to last about six weeks\, depending on weather. Expect 
 trenching and heavy equipment\, and brief water interruptions of under 30 
 minutes when homes are switched to a temporary line and again to the new o
 ne.\nThe six-week duration is approximate and depends on weather. Interrup
 tions are described as brief connection events\, not a continuous outage.
URL:https://www.waterauthority.ky/public-service-announcement-planned-works
 -rockshire-drive-pipeline-upgrade-and-relaying-project
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-a735d1c8ac6a280854ce@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:WORC offices in Grand Cayman and Cayman Brac close on 30 October
DESCRIPTION:WORC says its Grand Cayman and Cayman Brac offices will be clos
 ed Friday\, 30 October\, for a staff event. Regular office hours resume Mo
 nday\, 2 November.\nThe notice says regular hours resume on 2 November but
  does not state alternate service arrangements.
URL:https://gov.ky/noticeboard
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:notice-97781e4fc6ea6d90b1b4@n4mcayman.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T123902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:No school for students on Friday 4 December\; term ends 18 December
  at 1 pm
DESCRIPTION:4 December is a system-wide teacher training day. Government sc
 hools close for Christmas on 18 December\, when students leave at 1:00 pm.
  Term 2 starts on 4 January 2027.\n4 December is the single-day closure in
  this calendar entry\; 18 December is the separate term-end date. The appr
 oved PDF also gives a 4 January 2027 reopening. Confirm with your child's 
 school.
URL:https://gov.ky/w/cayman-islands-government-schools-2026-2027-school-cal
 endar
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
